EXT. MISSOURI RIVER FERRY LANDING - DUSK

A flat-bottomed ferry is chained to a cottonwood stump, rocking on brown water the width of a county. The sky has gone the colour of a bruise.

HOLLIS CRANE, lean and sun-cured, leans on the ferry rail. He wears a gun he has not touched in nine years. He watches the far bank without blinking.

A woman stands at the ramp with a carpetbag in each hand. PERPETUA VANCE, forty, black mourning dress, hat pinned hard. She sets down one bag. She keeps the other.

PERPETUA
You're the ferryman.

HOLLIS
Was.

He spits over the rail. The brown water takes it without comment.

PERPETUA
Then who is.

HOLLIS
Nobody. River's closed since the Tuesday flood. Company let us all go.

She looks at the chain. She looks at him. She says nothing, which is its own kind of answer.

She lifts the second bag and sets it on the plank between them. The latch is open a finger's width. Inside, the blued steel of a revolver catches the last light.

HOLLIS (CONT'D)
(quiet)
Ma'am.

PERPETUA
My husband crossed here a week ago. The man who took his fare. I'd like a word.

A shout rolls over the water from the far bank, flattened by distance.

ELIAS TWOCROWS (O.S.)
(hailing)
Hollis! Is that her? Is that the widow?

He does not turn. His jaw works. The hand that rests on the rail begins, very slowly, to slide toward his hip.

PERPETUA
Who is that?

HOLLIS
My brother.

ELIAS TWOCROWS (O.S.)
(nearer, a rifle bolt clacking)
Don't let her on the boat, Hollis!

She steps onto the ferry. The planks complain. She puts her hand on the bag.

PERPETUA
Then it was you who took the fare.

HOLLIS
I took it for him.

He draws. She draws. A crack splits the dusk, then another, and the cottonwood stump fountains bark. The chain snaps and the ferry lurches free, spinning into the current with the two of them still standing, still firing, on its drifting deck.
